WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:02.354
Meet Ampere.

2
00:00:02.354 --> 00:00:06.328
A menu bar battery manager for Apple Silicon Macs.

3
00:00:08.533 --> 00:00:13.811
Lithium-ion batteries age fastest when they sit at 100 percent, or drain near empty.

4
00:00:13.811 --> 00:00:18.272
A MacBook that lives on the charger spends most of its life at the top.

5
00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:23.471
Ampere holds your battery in a healthy range instead.

6
00:00:23.471 --> 00:00:25.631
Pick a band, like 40 to 60 percent.

7
00:00:25.631 --> 00:00:30.877
Charging starts at the bottom of the band, holds in the middle, and stops at the top.

8
00:00:30.877 --> 00:00:31.741
Automatically.

9
00:00:33.667 --> 00:00:37.891
The panel shows everything your battery wants you to know.

10
00:00:37.891 --> 00:00:40.586
Adapter, battery, and system wattage.

11
00:00:40.586 --> 00:00:45.684
Voltages, currents, temperature, cycle count, health, and battery age.

12
00:00:45.684 --> 00:00:48.088
A dozen readouts, always current.

13
00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:54.650
Between the bounds, charging stays off until you ask, even after a restart.

14
00:00:54.650 --> 00:00:59.920
Every cycle runs full, from the lower bound to the upper, with no fragmented top-ups.

15
00:01:01.833 --> 00:01:03.542
Heading out without a charger?

16
00:01:03.542 --> 00:01:09.920
Charge to Full tops the battery up in one tap, and normal management takes over again once the charge completes.

17
00:01:09.920 --> 00:01:11.686
Sitting above your upper bound?

18
00:01:11.686 --> 00:01:15.103
Discharge back down to it, even with the charger plugged in.

19
00:01:17.033 --> 00:01:25.121
Close the lid mid-charge, and Ampere pauses just before sleep and continues when your Mac wakes, so a charge never overshoots your bound.

20
00:01:25.121 --> 00:01:27.837
Quitting Ampere restores every system default.

21
00:01:27.837 --> 00:01:33.268
And if the app is ever force-killed, a watchdog puts your Mac back to normal within seconds.

22
00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:38.254
The menu bar icon shows your live charge level.

23
00:01:38.254 --> 00:01:42.803
Pin the panel open, or drag it off the menu bar and float it anywhere.

24
00:01:42.803 --> 00:01:45.077
Keep your Mac awake for a set time.

25
00:01:45.077 --> 00:01:46.117
Launch at login.

26
00:01:46.117 --> 00:01:47.936
Update right from the panel.

27
00:01:49.867 --> 00:01:53.536
Install it with Homebrew, or download the disk image.

28
00:01:53.536 --> 00:01:57.343
Grant admin once, set your bounds, and forget about it.

29
00:01:57.343 --> 00:02:01.012
Ampere is free in the default 40 to 60 percent range.

30
00:02:01.012 --> 00:02:03.851
A one-time license unlocks custom bounds.

31
00:02:05.967 --> 00:02:06.536
Ampere.

32
00:02:06.536 --> 00:02:08.811
Take charge of your battery.

33
00:02:08.811 --> 00:02:11.087
Get it at amperebattery.app.

